      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Sand Cave and White Rocks, nestled in Cumberland Gap National Historical Park, showcase rugged cliffs and winding mountain roads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heartsofappalachia.org/post/heartbeats-history-of-ewing-virginia",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ewing Covenant Brethren Church, founded in the early 20th century, remains a spiritual cornerstone of the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heartsofappalachia.org/post/heartbeats-history-of-ewing-virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Texaco station, recently restored, stands as a visual landmark honoring Ewing’s past while welcoming new travelers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heartsofappalachia.org/post/heartbeats-history-of-ewing-virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Thomas Walker High School opened in 1940, turning Ewing into a regional hub for education and trade after the railroad arrived.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heartsofappalachia.org/post/heartbeats-history-of-ewing-virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
